GH#492 candidate implementation -- NOT applied to production by this commit.

This is a normal development patch, not a build-time source transformer.
The source edits were authored against connection.rs blob
74e4bb5ee503fd40e0104dbbaa5dadabdef90777. The subsequently observed main blob
14e10e2384157c97d9d61629d52657b478d1cb6f includes peer changes: reconcile and
run git apply --check against a complete current checkout before applying.
Do not replace connection.rs from a partial fetch or overwrite peer edits.

Only optional prepared-read hydration is capped at an 8 MiB logical image.
Explicit correctness-required hydration keeps its existing boolean behavior.
The publication-bound check includes WAL growth; this is not an RSS budget or
an experimentally tuned crossover. FTS5 lazy admission stays independent.

The final two hunks activate the existing and WAL-growth ordinary regressions
in the keeper shipped with this patch. Apply the implementation and activation
together. Full-source application, compilation and engine tests have NOT run.
This artifact does not make #492 fixed or justify closing the issue.

Validation commands after applying to a complete checkout:
  cargo test -p fsqlite-core --test gh492_bounded_post_commit_hydration -- --nocapture
  cargo test -p fsqlite-core --test gh409_read_after_commit_scaling --test bd_xml0z_prepared_read_reload_and_eqp
  cargo check --workspace --all-targets
  cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
  cargo fmt --check

